data.content:
In .NET 10, `Microsoft.AspNetCore.OpenApi` upgraded to **Microsoft.OpenApi v2**, which targets OpenAPI 3.1. Here are the key breaking changes and fixes:

## What Changed

| .NET 9 (OpenApi v1) | .NET 10 (OpenApi v2) |
|---|---|
| `Microsoft.OpenApi.Any.OpenApiString` etc. | Removed — use `System.Text.Json.Nodes.JsonNode` |
| `schema.Nullable = true/false` | Removed — use `schema.Type` with `JsonSchemaType.Null` flag |
| `OpenApiSecurityRequirement` is a `Dictionary<OpenApiSecurityScheme, IList<string>>` | Now has explicit properties (`Schemes` dictionary) |
| `new OpenApiReference { Type = ReferenceType.SecurityScheme, Id = "..." }` | `ReferenceType` → `ReferenceType.SecurityScheme` still exists but `Type` is now non-nullable and the constructor pattern changed |

## Fixed Code

```csharp
using System.Text.Json.Nodes;
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Models;

options.AddOperationTransformer((operation, context, ct) =>
{
    var param = operation.Parameters.FirstOrDefault(p => p.Name == "api-version");
    if (param is not null)
    {
        // OpenApiString is gone; use JsonNode instead
        param.Schema.Example = JsonValue.Create("1.0");
    }

    operation.Responses ??= new Dictionary<string, OpenApiResponse>();
    operation.Responses.TryAdd("401", new OpenApiResponse { Description = "Unauthorized" });

    var oAuthScheme = new OpenApiSecurityScheme
    {
        Reference = new OpenApiReference { Type = ReferenceType.SecurityScheme, Id = "oauth2" }
    };

    // OpenApiSecurityRequirement is no longer a dictionary itself;
    // use its Schemes property instead
    var requirement = new OpenApiSecurityRequirement();
    requirement.Schemes.Add(oAuthScheme, scopes);

    operation.Security = [requirement];

    return Task.CompletedTask;
});

options.AddSchemaTransformer((schema, context, ct) =>
{
    if (schema.Properties is not null)
    {
        foreach (var property in schema.Properties)
        {
            if (schema.Required?.Contains(property.Key) != true)
            {
                // .Nullable is removed in OpenAPI 3.1; instead remove the
                // "null" option from the type flags to make it non-nullable
                property.Value.Type &= ~JsonSchemaType.Null;
            }
        }
    }
    return Task.CompletedTask;
});
```

## Summary of fixes

1. **`OpenApiString` → `JsonValue.Create("1.0")`** — all `OpenApi*` primitive types replaced by `System.Text.Json.Nodes`.
2. **`Nullable = false` → `Type &= ~JsonSchemaType.Null`** — OpenAPI 3.1 expresses nullability via the `type` array.
3. **`new() { [scheme] = scopes }` → `requirement.Schemes.Add(scheme, scopes)`** — `OpenApiSecurityRequirement` no longer implements `IDictionary` directly.
